Z80MODE                                                        [3.0]
-------

Format:      Z80MODE slot[-subslot] [ON | OFF]

Purpose:     Displays or sets the Z80 access mode of a  legacy  disk
        driver.

Use:         The slot argument selects the disk driver to operate
        on:  a primary slot number (0 to 3),  followed by a dash and
        a subslot number when the slot is expanded.  A plain 0 means
        the slot of the master disk ROM.

             If no ON or OFF is given,  the current  state  of   the
        mode  for that driver is displayed;  otherwise the  mode  is
        enabled or disabled.

             While the mode is enabled,  Nextor switches the CPU  to
        Z80 mode before every access to the driver and restores  the
        previous CPU mode afterwards.  This allows  legacy   MSX-DOS
        drivers that are not compatible with the R800 CPU to work on
        an MSX Turbo-R.

             The mode exists on the MSX Turbo-R  only,  and only for
        MSX-DOS (legacy) drivers:  for any other machine  or  driver
        'Invalid device driver' is reported.

Examples:

        Z80MODE 1
        OFF

             The mode is currently disabled for the  driver  in slot
        1.

        Z80MODE 3-2 ON

             The mode is enabled for the driver in slot 3-2.
